## The model: 2014 to 2025
In 2025 UWPHI introduced a new model of health, evolved from the 2014 CHR model. Its four components are:
*   **Population Health and Well-being**, which replaces “Health Outcomes” and adds well-being, including quality of life;  
*   **Community Conditions**, which replaces “Health Factors”;  
*   **Societal Rules**, the written and unwritten rules that shape community conditions;  
*   **Power**, the ability to achieve a purpose and effect change.
The new model also introduces constructs for health promotion and harm reduction, climate, and civic and community resources. CHR&R states nominal weights for the two components that have summary measures: within Population Health and Well-being, Length of Life 50% and Quality of Life 50%; within Community Conditions, Health Infrastructure 25%, Physical Environment 25% and Social and Economic Factors 50%. Component measures are standardized to z-scores and combined using those weights. The program states there is currently no summary measure for Societal Rules or Power.
